course: dictionary
lesson: 4664
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The word hog can be a naming word for an animal, or a doing word that means to keep something for yourself. Read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: «Kitti's hog-nosed bat, the bumblebee bat of Thailand and Myanmar, weighs about 2 grams.» Here hog is part of an animal's name, and the word is the same as the word for a pig. Check the rest of the sentence before you decide what it means.
explain: Hog can also describe a person. Someone who is greedy or selfish, and keeps more than their share, can be called a hog. If a friend will not let anyone else have a turn, the word hog fits them.
explain: Some phrases use hog in a special way. «Go the whole hog» does not mean anything about pigs. Read the whole phrase together, because the meaning often comes from all the words working as one.
fact: A hog is a pig, often a large one kept on a farm.
fact: Hog can be a verb: to hog something means to keep it all to yourself and not share it.
fact: A road hog is an informal word for a greedy or selfish person.
fact: «Go the whole hog» means do something completely.
fact: «Kitti's hog-nosed bat» weighs about 2 grams and is one of the smallest mammals, along with the Etruscan shrew.
exercise: What is a hog? | A flower that grows in gardens | A car with a loud horn | *A pig, often a large one kept on a farm | A bird that sings at dawn
exercise: Ella says, «Don't hog the ball!» What does hog mean here? | *To keep the ball all to yourself and not share it | To kick the ball very far | To lose the ball in the grass | To give the ball to everyone
exercise: «He decided to go the whole hog and paint the entire house in one day.» What does go the whole hog mean? | Run to the end of a field | Stop and have a rest | *Do something completely | Eat a big dinner
test: «He is such a road hog that he never lets anyone else have a turn.» What does road hog mean here? | A quiet friend | *A greedy or selfish person | A slow driver who is kind | A pig living by the road
test: «Kitti's bat weighs about 2 grams.» What does this tell you about the bat? | *It is very light, one of the smallest mammals | It is bigger than a pig | It weighs as much as a bicycle | It is one of the heaviest animals
exam: Which sentence uses hog as a verb? | «Kitti's bat weighs about 2 grams.» | «The farmer keeps a hog in the barn.» | «The hedgehog curled into a ball.» | *«Tom tried to hog the remote all evening.»
